<title>INDIA: Oil India 96/97 net 2.10 billion rupees.</title>
<headline>Oil India 96/97 net 2.10 billion rupees.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-04-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-run Oil India Ltd (OIL) said on Saturday its net profit increased to 2.10 billion rupees in 1996/97 (April-March) from 2.06 billion in 1995/96.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement it produced crude oil &quot;nearer to the last year's level&quot; and surpassed the liquified petroleum gas (LPG) production target set for 1996/97. It did not give details.</p>
<p>The government holds a 97 percent stake in OIL, with the remaining three percent held by its employees.</p>
<p>OIL is India's second largest oil producer after state-run Oil and Natural Gas Corp.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
